          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Lorck\",\"addressee\":\"Constance\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Lorck directly avows to Constance that he is in a loving emotional state. The surrounding claim that it is serious reinforces the truth-presenting force, regardless of whether the feeling is sincere.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"det er Alvor\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The focal expression itself reports love but does not specify an undertaking, obligation, or promised course of action. Lorck's immediately following offer of himself, his life, and his soul has separate commitment-like force and is not transferred onto the marked expression.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"Although Lorck speaks in an emotionally charged confrontation, the focal words are a deliberate, propositionally framed avowal rather than a reflex-like discharge of affect. Emotional intensity alone does not establish expressive-discharge force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"det er Alvor\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The focal expression's core force is adequately represented as an avowal of a loving state; no distinct residual function beyond T is established for these exact words.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After Constance rejects Lorck's advances and reacts fearfully, Lorck confronts her and directly declares his love. The declaration occurs as part of a longer appeal in which he offers himself, his life, and his soul and asks whether she will accept them. Constance answers negatively and retreats.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The marked expression itself contains no undertaking. In the neighbouring sentence, Lorck offers Constance himself, his life, and his soul and asks her to accept; the terms are highly rhetorical and nonspecific. Constance explicitly rejects the offer with “Nej, uf nej” and moves away, so there is no uptake.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passage identifies the work as Amalie Skram's Constance Ring.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage supports interpreting Lorck's declaration as an avowal and supplies behavioural signs of intense passion, but it cannot conclusively establish the sincerity, durability, or precise nature of his affection. The separate offer that follows must not be treated as part of the focal expression's force.\"}"
        }
